Phase 41, Plan 41-08, Task 1 (E41-8/FILL-04) -- 127.0.0.1:8770 chosen as the third-party domain
after a first, failed run at a fresh `.localhost` subdomain never propagated to QuickType across
4 retried attempts -- isolated to L-38 (`ios/IOS-SPIKE-LOG.md`), a live addition to E41-3's own
unresolved Falsification-3 finding. 127.0.0.1 is loopback, not a registrable DNS domain: no
publicly-trusted TLS cert can ever be issued for it and Apple's own AASA fetch mechanism could
never retrieve a site-association file for it -- "no site-association file could exist" holds by
construction, and it is clearly not a domain this product controls.

## Falsification (acceptance criteria): expected password altered by one character, re-run,
## observe failure, restored, re-run, observe pass again
Temporarily changed the TEST's own `expectedPassword` constant by one character (the trailing
character only), leaving the REAL seeded/filled password unchanged (T-41-12/T-41-15: never
reproducing the literal plaintext password value in this evidence file):
  $ bash scripts/ios-autofill-e41.sh e41-8
  PVUITEST|E41-8|host=127.0.0.1 port=8770 attempt=1 status=filled-on-attempt
  XCODEBUILD-EXIT: 65
  FAIL: e41-8 -- no field-value-equal=true line found in ios/evidence/41/e41-8-thirdparty.log
The extension's own os_log for this run confirms the ACTUAL fill still succeeded internally
(`PVFILL|entry=silent stage=fill status=ok`) -- the failure is purely the test's own
`XCTAssertEqual` catching the deliberately-wrong expectation, exactly as intended
(`continueAfterFailure = false` stops the test before the `field-value-equal=...` print line ever
runs, which is why that line is absent rather than printed `false`).
Reverted the one-character change and re-ran: PASS (see below), confirming a clean restoration.

